---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
---

<Base
  title="How to cite"
  description="How to cite the AI Reg. Index: entry, comparison, and dataset citation formats, and the CC BY 4.0 attribution string."
  path="/cite/"
  nav={null}
>
  <PageHeader
    kicker="Attribution"
    title="How to cite"
    intro="Register text is licensed CC BY 4.0. Cite the entry, not just the site, so a reader can check the same source and verification date you used."
  />

  <div class="sec">
    <h2 class="h2">A register entry</h2>
    <div class="cite-box">
      AI Reg. Index. &ldquo;EU AI Act: Article 50 &mdash; Transparency &amp;
      Synthetic Media Disclosures.&rdquo; &sect; 8.
      airegindex.com/sources/eu-ai-act-article-50-transparency-and-synthetic-media-disclosures.
      Last verified 30 July 2026.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec">
    <h2 class="h2">A comparison</h2>
    <div class="cite-box">
      AI Reg. Index. &ldquo;Automated decision-making disclosure laws (United
      States).&rdquo; airegindex.com/comparisons. Retrieved 5 September 2026.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec">
    <h2 class="h2">The dataset</h2>
    <div class="cite-box">
      AI Reg. Index [dataset]. airegindex.com/register.json. Retrieved 5
      September 2026.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sec">
    <h2 class="h2">Notes</h2>
    <p class="body-text">
      Each entry has a permanent URL built from its jurisdiction and short
      name; the URL does not change when the entry is re-verified. The primary
      documents themselves are the property of the governments and standards
      bodies that publish them &mdash; cite those directly when you can.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
